wly reveals more of shazam's new suit  we can see that it's definitely an  upgrade from his costume in the last  movie where his first suit was more of a  classic comic accurate version this one  is like 200 less dorky while he  confesses his origin story to his doctor  we flash back to scenes from the first  movie when billy first gained his new  powers back at the group home darla  eugene pedro freddy mary and billy are  gearing up to fight crime when they're  stopped and questioned by their foster  parents victor and rosa vazquez a few  t-shirts here might catch your eye billy  is wearing goonies merch back during the  press interviews for the first shazam  zachary levi fondly compared his movie  with spielberg's 1985 classic seeing the  goonies referenced in fury of the gods  might reflect that this outing will lean  further into the shazam family being a  band of child adventurers on a quest to  protect their home freddy's shirt sports  the symbol of the white tree of gondor  from lord of the rings this tree  symbolizes hope and the renewal of life  and even though freddie is more of billy  samwise than an aragorn this optimistic  pop culture reference is the perfect  encapsulation of the character then we  have gamer boy eugene who is wearing an  iconoclast shirt featuring robin the  silent protagonist of the 2018 game like  robin eugene has an affinity towards  technology also iconoclasts was  developed by director david f sandberg's  brother while billy's voice over  explains that everyone in the shazam ali  is now off doing their own things we see  the grown-up superhero versions of these  characters as they land on  philadelphia's benjamin franklin bridge  their suits like shazams have also been  upgraded since the last time we saw them  and this time mary aka actor grace  caroline curry doesn't transform into  actor michelle bort in this movie she's  playing herself as an adult hero because  she and the rest of the actors have all  grown since they filmed the first shazam  it turns out that shazam isn't pouring  his heart out to a therapist he's  actually at the office of an extremely  confused pediatrician who clearly didn't  specialize in children being trapped  inside zachary levi's muscular body  during med school this doctor's office  is full of easter eggs in the play area  we see three wonder woman dolls a batman  doll a flash doll a batman action figure  and two bears dressed as robin and green  lantern the abc wallpaper features three  characters from within the dceu and dc  comics k for caroquan an ancient sea  monster from aquaman comics s for starro  the giant starfish kaiju that fought  james guns the suicide squad and t for  titiano's super ape a gigantic ape with  evil kryptonite powers from superman  comics returning for her third debut in  the dceu the doll from annabelle can  also be seen chillin at the  pediatricians david f sandberg the  director of both shazam movies was also  the director of annabelle creation you  can spot the creepy doll at the  beginning of the first movie inside of  the pawn shop before billy locks the two  cops inside likewise james wan the  writer of aquaman worked as a producer  on the conjuring 2 annabelle and  annabelle creation you can also see that  scary little freak right where she  belongs in a pile of trash at the bottom  of the ocean in aquaman next we see this  large palatial structure beneath the  swirling looming sky that actually kind  of reminds me of mount olympus from  greek mythology i think that this shot  definitely takes place in the realm of  the gods a location that producer peter  saffron mentioned back in a teaser from  2021. he said quote we go from athens to  philadelphia we go from the rock of  eternity to the library of eternity to  the realm of the gods i think that this  structure could be home to the film's  antagonists the daughters of atlas in  the same way that mount olympus was home  to zeus and the other gods and  mythological tales as we learned in the  first film the rock of eternity is the  wizard's lair so my next logical guess  is that this room that appears towards  the end of the trailer is the library of  eternity in athens greece we briefly see  the acropolis atop the hill of the muses  before being taken inside a local museum  where the daughters of atlas hespera and  calypso are removing their traditional  greek battle helmets in preparation for  a heist played by dame helen miriam and  lucy liu hespera and calypso's  characters are unique to fury of the  gods they don't appear in dc comics  instead both are inspired by nymphs from  greek mythology hespera is based on the  hesperides three nymphs of dawn and dusk  tasked with protecting the golden apple  tree in harrah's garden interestingly in  the teaser from 2021 we see hespera  clutching a monotone black apple which  could be a nod to the fact that the gods  and their gardens have lost their magic  to the shazamily calypso was influenced  by calypso the nymph most notable for  trapping odysseus on her island agaija  for seven years in homer's the odyssey  both are daughters of the titan atlas a  pre-olympian god cursed to hold the  heavens on his shoulders for eternity as  they prepare to steal the staff that  shazam broke in half in the first movie  you can see a sculpture of atlas holding  the globe in the background atlas does  appear as a character in dc comics and  was even one of shazam's antagonists and  the infected king shazam but based on  what we know about fury of the gods  we're gonna see more mythology the comic  book lore from the villains in this film  during a panel at comic con rachel  zegler confirmed that her character  would be the third daughter of atlas and  thea oddly enough anthea isn't one of  atlas's daughters in greek mythology nor  does she appear anywhere in dc comics  she's technically a thespian princess  daughter of king thespias and megameen  mother to one of heracles children when  hespera first removes her helmet is it  just me or does her right eye seem a lot  brighter blue than her left when the eye  of sins flew into dr savannah's face  hole in the last movie his right eye  also glowed like an evil lava lamp when  his sparrow reaches out and grasps the  broken staff a lightning bolt seemingly  ignites beneath her skin illuminating  her eyes and reawakening the staff's  magic in spite of shazam's previous  efforts to destroy it the next time we  see the staff calypso is holding it  glowing and intact next to her sisters  notice that anthea is standing apart  from her sisters another hint that the  third daughter of atlas might be more  sympathetic towards humanity than  hespera and calypso freddie's also  present here and is seen with anthea  quite a lot in this trailer leading me  to believe that this young goddess might  fall in love with humanity through a  romance with freddy they also hold hands  here while being attacked by the dragon  later on in the trailer another shot  later on has anthea blasted backwards by  a beam of blue lightning this must have  come from the staff because shazam's  lightning is white meaning it's likely  that her sisters will turn on her here  hesphera tells us that children stole  power from all of the gods seemingly  referring to when billy decided to share  shazam's powers with his foster siblings  in 1940s whiz comics number two each of  the powers that the wizard shazam  bestows on billy batson are drawn from  seven greek gods and heroes s for  solomon's wisdom h for hercules strength  a for atlas's stamina z for zeus's power  a for achilles courage and m for mercury  speed perhaps in fury of the gods it'll  turn out that billy stole or diluted  these god's powers when he transferred  part of his magic to darla eugene pedro  freddy and mary this is also a nod to  the myth of prometheus in which the  titan prometheus stole fire from the  gods and gave it to humanity zeus  punished prometheus by chaining him to a  rock 